<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luchino dal Verme</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1320–1372</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luchino dal Verme was an Italian condottiero from Verona who served the Visconti of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> and the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. In 1364 Venice hired him to command the army that put down the Revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titus-saint">Saint Titus</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, and he retook <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraklion">Candia</a> in May of that year. He later fought for Venice against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and died in 1372.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luchino-dal-verme.jpg" alt="Luchino dal Verme" width="320" height="366" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tettoni-Saladini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stemma_Dal_Verme.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
